{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, allow SSH only for ssh-access members using public-key authentication, while denying direct root access, contractor access, and password-based authentication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final effective policy has AllowGroups ssh-access, AuthenticationMethods publickey, PermitRootLogin no, DenyUsers contractor, and password/keyboard-interactive authentication disabled. Final and post-restart tests show opsadmin succeeds while root, contractor, and password-only attempts fail.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b1dd268dd4104842","cmd-f39d404e3f444c26","cmd-f0ea4adfd1b84e96"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide the prepared opsadmin account with source-pinned, non-interactive key access from sshprobe on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The existing key fingerprint was retained and its authorization was restricted to node2's 10.100.242.11 source with restrict. Strict host-key-checked BatchMode access from sshprobe succeeds, while forced PTY allocation fails, including after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ef033aed6d9431d","cmd-f39d404e3f444c26","cmd-da5a62a294db4729"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Use the dedicated ssh-admin firewalld zone for the jump-box boundary, permitting node2 while denying node3 network access to node1 SSH.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final runtime and permanent state place 10.100.242.11/32 with SSH in ssh-admin and remove SSH from public. Node2 retains functional SSH access, while node3 receives a network-layer rejection before and after restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-db5c01a6dd364804","cmd-b1dd268dd4104842","cmd-f39d404e3f444c26","cmd-b6fe8e4d276d4348","cmd-d29f19cb0d5f4d93"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the prepared accounts, keys, and data.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"Final evidence verifies the opsadmin and contractor identities, memberships, home data, contractor key, retained opsadmin key fingerprint, and node2 sshprobe credentials and data digest after restart. However, node3's prepared sshprobe account, key, and known_hosts were not re-observed after its restart; node1's root authorized key and prepared shadow checksum were also not rechecked.","evidence_ids":["prepared-target-state","prepared-jump-box","prepared-untrusted-client","cmd-7dbc097153924628","cmd-b1dd268dd4104842","cmd-da5a62a294db4729"]}],"confidence":0.92,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The configuration, key restriction, reloads, firewall changes, transient verification files, and required restart actions all have clear task or evidence roles. Temporary /run public-key files were removed. The only unwanted retained residue is /root/opsadmin-authorized_keys.pre-hardening: it was a reasonable rollback copy when created but no later cleanup is captured, so it remained as an unnecessary final backup. No failed services, package damage, or unexpected socket changes were observed after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ef033aed6d9431d","cmd-b3a317656fca400b","cmd-da5a62a294db4729","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The SSH hardening and jump-box firewall boundary are directly demonstrated and remained functional after node1 and node2 restarts. Every managed node has a pre-restart boot identity, restart acknowledgement, different post-restart identity, and recovered services/role behavior; the fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree. The provider restart protocol is incomplete only for node3 data recovery, which also leaves the broad preservation outcome partially demonstrated rather than fully satisfied.","limitations":["Node3 restart evidence verifies boot change, services, addressing, routing, and continued network denial, but does not verify recovery of its prepared sshprobe account, key, or known_hosts (cmd-2af36a6eb75a494a; cmd-bc07473d737c4d77).","Node1 final preservation evidence does not revalidate /root/.ssh/authorized_keys or the prepared shadow checksum, although no captured mutation targets either item.","The initial node2 private/public-key comparison reported a mismatch and a follow-up comparison failed because they compared differing textual field forms; later exact-file and fingerprint checks resolved the contradiction (cmd-56a4c6988bbf495d; cmd-c5c1728700ed43e6; cmd-b3a317656fca400b; cmd-da5a62a294db4729).","The final authorized_keys option display is partially redacted, so the exact source restriction is established through the captured write command and corroborating source-specific behavior rather than a clean final raw-line observation."]}
